{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0y98qt","slide":3,"text":"Explain the product in one sweep: Fireworks extracts the behavioral claim and designs attacks; Daytona executes those attacks against both revisions; CodeRabbit supplies a separate review opinion. Braintrust traces the decision, CopilotKit makes it explorable, and the human owns the final call.\n\n[Sources]\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/lib/pipeline.ts — orchestrated claim, evidence, comparison, and recommendation flow\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/lib/adapters/fireworks.ts — claim extraction and adversarial test generation\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/lib/adapters/daytona.ts — isolated before/after execution\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/app/api/copilotkit/[...slug]/route.ts — CopilotKit runtime"}
